# MiladyOS ISO — text installer (replaces the Calamares GUI session).
# The installer copies the live rootfs to disk itself; these are the tools
# it needs in the live environment.

# --- TUI ---
# gum is the installer's UI (matrix palette + centered ASCII banner).
# dialog is kept as a fallback (MILADY_UI=dialog) for scripted serial
# automation and older media.
gum
dialog

# --- disk + filesystems ---
parted
gdisk
dosfstools
e2fsprogs
util-linux

# --- copy ---
rsync

# --- bootloader (UEFI + BIOS) ---
grub-common
grub-pc-bin
grub-efi-amd64-bin
efibootmgr
initramfs-tools
kmod

# --- branding ---
# `milady-install` measures the banner with `wc -L`, which needs a UTF-8
# locale to count characters rather than bytes; C.UTF-8 is built into glibc.
# (no extra packages: coreutils/sed/grep come with the base system)
